      "manifest_record": "generated-input-approval.json",
      "manifest_schema": "p08-generated-input-approval-1",
      "output_execution": "Only the exact generated entries and commands independently accepted in this new M may be invoked",
      "prior_compilation_result": "One authenticated SUCCESS_ELIGIBLE_OUTPUTS B and its exact signature are mandatory",
      "source_acceptance": "The same active accepted S may be reused; fresh M/R/O/G identities are mandatory"
    }
  },
  "canonical_byte_rules": {
    "compilation_result_max_bytes": 8192,
    "duplicate_keys": "REJECT_BEFORE_MAP_CONVERSION",
    "encoding": "ASCII subset of UTF-8",
    "final_newline": false,
    "generated_grant_max_bytes": 8192,
    "generated_manifest_max_bytes": 16384,
    "json_null_boolean_array_object_values": "FORBIDDEN",
    "key_order": "strict ascending ASCII bytes",
    "manifest_max_bytes": 16384,
    "nested_values_in_five_records": "FORBIDDEN",
    "numbers": "minimal unsigned decimal, u64 only; 0 allowed, leading zeros forbidden",
    "other_record_max_bytes": 8192,
    "sha256": "lowercase hexadecimal over exact bytes",
    "sshsig_max_bytes": 4096,
    "string_bytes": "0x20..0x7e excluding quote and backslash; field constraints may narrow further",
    "string_escapes": "FORBIDDEN",
    "unknown_or_missing_fields": "REJECT",
    "whitespace": "NONE"
  },
  "cross_record_requirements": [
    "Source commit is a distinct reviewed successor with exactly C0 as parent. Only the identity-test file may differ; source tree and full inventory must reproduce it.",
    "Every profile, report, signature and source-stage acceptance reference resolves to exact actual bytes. All-zero identities are invalid.",
    "Issuer and reviewer must match the two distinct independently enrolled keys, roles and namespaces in the separately owner-accepted trust profile.",
    "S must authenticate under the owner role and source-stage namespace, bind exact C0 commit/tree/parent, source-preparation-only scope and the reviewed archive. M/R/O must all name SHA-256(S), the same accepted trust profile and consistent issuer/reviewer roles; G must name the accepted M/R/O chain. Retain S and its signature under independent custody. A source-acceptance digest alone is invalid.",
    "For every observed_* field in G require equality with the corresponding M identity; source commit/tree must equal M. Resolve the execution profile named by M.execution_profile_sha256, find the command-profile entry with SHA-256 equal to G.command_profile_sha256, and require its authorization_scope to equal G.authorization_scope exactly.",
    "For each record with not_before require issued_at <= not_before < expires_at. R requires issued_at < expires_at. All issue times must be no later than the independent current time uncertainty interval.",
    "M/R/O lifetime is no more than the approved input-age limit. G lifetime and max_duration_s are nonzero and no more than the approved lease limit. G interval and maximum run fit entirely inside all applicable M/R/O and key/profile validity intervals.",
    "The independent bounded current-time interval must lie entirely within every applicable active validity interval. No blanket after-expiry skew grace is allowed. Signed timestamps alone do not establish current time.",
    "G current status report must match the latest independent trust epoch, active enrollment and decisions and the action run ID. External atomic nonce consumption and custody are mandatory before launch.",
    "Preflight has separately accepted actual full source/tool/image observations, no missing closure/controls and Policy A status. The in-test signature checks cannot substitute for that external evidence.",
    "Source-stage S has no execution permission and no renewable time lease. Its exact decision remains subject to current revocation/status and accepted key status. Require S.issued_at <= M.issued_at, R.issued_at and O.issued_at.",
    "M.sbom_sha256 and M.license_inventory_sha256 must equal the respective fields of the resolved build-image profile. Those inventories must cover the complete approved build inputs, including sealed source and mounted toolchain/library inputs; a publisher image-only SBOM is insufficient.",
    "Every executable and installed component entry point resolves through a closed installed_artifact to its exact approved path, inventory digest and path/endpoint entry identities. Apply all installed_artifact_rules. Require actual exec path and argv[0] equal path and observed resolution equal resolved_path. No search by digest, PATH fallback or undeclared symlink can satisfy this binding.",
    "R.review_observation_sha256 authenticates only the closed INPUT_REVIEW_ONLY report, with matching review_id/reviewer/manifest/source/profile identities and review-time freshness. It contains no future run/grant identity and never authorizes launch.",
    "G.action_observation_sha256 authenticates only the closed ACTION_PREFLIGHT_ONLY report. Match grant_id/run_id/nonce/M/O/R/trust/command/scope/source and every observed profile identity to G. Use the independent external observation, clock and launch checks in profile-requirements.json.",
    "Fresh action observations must satisfy the owner-approved monotonic observation-to-launch maximum, proposed 60 seconds, in the same external clock session. The check is after signing/queue delay immediately before launch. Review observations cannot substitute, even if their hashes and inputs still match.",
    "Stale, wrong-purpose, wrong-run, missing or unauthenticated action evidence refuses before launch and terminally records the G/nonce. New observation and new grant/run/nonce are mandatory for another proposed action. Do not treat input approval age or the action lease as freshness."
  ],
  "description": "Closed field/type descriptors. Stage selection, receipt provenance, byte rules, cross-record checks and profile/lifecycle rules are mandatory. No approval instance or validator implementation is supplied.",
  "generated_stage_rules": [
    "An approval bundle has exactly one M and one matching G type from approval_stages. S, R and O retain their exact existing schemas and signature purposes. Unsupported or mixed-stage shapes refuse; a valid signature on the wrong stage is insufficient.",
    "Original S/M_build/R/O/G_build bodies are unchanged. M_build can select only BUILD_ONLY or INDEPENDENT_REBUILD commands. Its output expectations may name roles/layout but cannot contain predicted generated executable identities or authorize their execution.",
    "B is an authenticated historical compilation-result attestation, not input approval or execution permission. The existing enrolled independent reviewer signs B under symphony.p08.build-result.v1 only after independently verifying the producer chain, actual zero exit, audits, exact outputs and immutable custody. No third signing role or self-issued build receipt is introduced.",
    "B must match the exact consumed successful producer G and its M/R/O/signatures, source, command, IDs and nonce. started_at <= completed_at <= issued_at, and producer authorization/lease/status/effects must have remained valid for the action. Failed, interrupted, ambiguous, out-of-scope or unsealed attempts cannot issue eligible B, even if some output bytes exist.",
    "Each M_test uses the generated-input schema and a new approval_id. compilation_result_sha256 and compilation_result_signature_sha256 identify exact B and its authentic signature. Require M_test.generated_inputs_profile_sha256 == B.generated_inputs_profile_sha256 == SHA-256(Q). The profile source and producer identities must match B and M_test. One B per new M_test is supported in this bounded contract; separate producer actions use separate approval cycles.",
    "Fresh R_test with a new review_id must independently inspect the new M_test, B/signature, raw evidence, installed output entries, immutable custody and current status. Fresh O_test with a new decision_id must explicitly accept SHA-256(M_test) and R_test. R_build/O_build, B alone or compilation success never substitutes.",
    "M_test preserves the exact accepted source/tree/frozen files and S. Actual compiler/target/CRT/linker input identities and the tools-only OCI manifest/platform/layers remain bound to the producer. Its execution, generated-input custody, SBOM/licenses and current evidence profiles are independently reviewed anew; no unrelated source/tool/environment change is authorized by this transition.",
    "G_test must be the generated-native-grant schema, bind only the newly active M_test/R_test/O_test chain and an exact command already in M_test execution_profile. Its executable must equal one of the generated profile installed_artifact entries in every field and be in the new child allowlist. Its scope is one permitted test action. A base build grant or compilation receipt cannot execute it.",
    "G_test.observed_generated_inputs_profile_sha256 equals M_test.generated_inputs_profile_sha256. The fresh ACTION_PREFLIGHT_ONLY report includes the generated_inputs role in profiles and matches that identity plus all other M/G observations. Existing F01 installed path/chain rules and F02 run/nonce/clock/freshness/status/lease/one-use rules apply unchanged.",
    "Historical producer G is expected to be consumed and successful. Its later expiry is not a new execution grant and does not erase provenance; verify its historical validity and current disqualifying status. Only the fresh M_test/R_test/O_test/G_test supplies current permission. Revoked, invalid or unverifiable producer provenance/custody blocks descendants.",
    "The references are acyclic: G_build precedes output inventory/custody and raw compilation evidence E; generated profile Q references E and the inventory/custody, never B or M_test; B references E and Q; M_test references B/signature/Q; R_test then O_test then G_test reference only prior records. Generated installed_artifact.provenance_sha256 equals E, never B, preventing a B/Q hash cycle.",
    "The same fresh-approval rule applies before any subsequent command invokes an executable generated after its current M was accepted. Reading outputs as data with separately approved inspection tools does not execute them. New actions outside the existing T04 test scopes still require separate authority.",
    "B.completed_at equals E.completed_at; B.issued_at is no earlier than C.sealed_at and completed_at. B and M_test source/producer/evidence/profile references agree exactly. M_test.issued_at is no earlier than B.issued_at. Reviewer key/status must authorize B at attestation and current provenance checks.",
    "Generated executable roles are restricted to codec_test and locked_build_identity. Client/helper runtime stubs remain data-only outputs, never permitted generated test targets.",
    "B.reviewer_id equals the producer M reviewer and the enrolled reviewer principal. B.operator_id equals the appointed producer/custody operator; B.trust_profile_sha256 equals producer M and M_test. E/Q/C producer IDs and inventories agree with B. A different key, operator, profile, action or output set cannot be selected by matching hashes alone.",
    "The B attestor and fresh R_test reviewer use the existing enrolled independent-reviewer role and remain independent of the build guest, implementation preparer and producer action operator. No new signing role is created. If actual role/custody separation is unavailable, attestation/input review remains blocked rather than self-certified.",
    "An eligible producer command must actually compile the exact expected test targets into its fresh granted output roots. Successful inspection-only commands, unrelated successful builds, stale cached binaries or mere output existence cannot produce Q/B for a target."
  ],
